# Different evasion abilities are cumulative (CR 509.1b): Callous Inspector has menace ("can't be blocked except by two or more
# creatures", CR 702.110b) and, enchanted by Meltstrider's Resolve, "can't be blocked by more than one creature", so no
# declaration can block it. Bot2 may block it neither with one creature nor with two; its Curious Farm Animals blocks the other
# attacker, Elvish Mystic, instead (the positive control: Bot2 is asked to declare blockers). The Inspector's 1 damage gets
# through.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Callous Inspector
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Meltstrider's Resolve
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Curious Farm Animals
Haywire Mite
Plains x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Callous Inspector.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Curious Farm Animals.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Haywire Mite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Meltstrider's Resolve.Cast(Callous Inspector)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target()
? Bot1.Battlefield.Callous Inspector.Keywords = CantBeBlockedByMoreThanOne; Menace
[T5 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Callous Inspector; Elvish Mystic > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Haywire Mite > Callous Inspector)
! Bot2.Block(Curious Farm Animals > Callous Inspector; Haywire Mite > Callous Inspector)
Bot2.Block(Curious Farm Animals > Elvish Mystic)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 22
Bot1.Graveyard = Elvish Mystic
Bot2.Graveyard = Curious Farm Animals
